From 4932b85ff63173a04267e4690192c6ee63097c0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kaesi0 <kaesi0@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:06:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(audio): play a network audio URL in the notification
 state

Adds Application::PlayAudioUrl(url) for the board MCP tool
self.audio.play_url, entering the official Notifying state so the cloud's
session teardown cannot abort the download (see the fw-14 serial trace: entering
Speaking runs ResetDecoder and the download task abandons the stream).

This revision also closes three review findings:

- OnAudioChannelClosed no longer drops the radio to LOW_POWER when a story is
  playing. That call sat outside the Notifying guard, so the remaining minutes
  of a story downloaded under Wi-Fi modem sleep - the very condition that makes
  NotifyPlayer log underruns. The downgrade now happens in StopNotification()
  when the story actually ends.
- PlayAudioUrl no longer destroys the current playback when the previous
  download is merely winding down (IsBusy() but not IsActive()): there is
  nothing to take over, so it fails fast and leaves the device as it was instead
  of stopping the old story and then failing to start a new one.
- A https url now logs a clear warning. TLS record buffers need 16749 contiguous
  bytes and this board has no PSRAM (largest free block during playback is
  7.7~17 KB), so https audio aborts mid-stream; the log now says so instead of
  leaving "Connection closed prematurely" as a dead end.

Constraint from the firmware: mono Ogg Opus, logical packets <= 2048 bytes,
no redirects, 2xx only.
---
 main/application.cc | 147 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 main/application.h  |  17 +++++
 2 files changed, 161 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

